Tasks: Template the Scala source (both Phase 2 tasks - main and test)

Summary:
Ported all 7 main source files and all 10 test files (including the
examples/ package) from src/{main,test}/scala/orderservice into
src/main/g8/src/{main,test}/scala/$package$/, with identifiers renamed via
$domain_name;format="cap"$ (Order -> Widget, OrderStore -> WidgetStore, etc.)
and repackaged via the independently-settable $package$ property.

Two environment/tooling discoveries along the way, both now documented in the
commit message and (for the escaping one) worth remembering for any future
giter8 work:
1. giter8's capitalize-first-letter format name is lowercase "cap", not "Cap"
   as I'd assumed - an unrecognized format name is silently ignored (falls
   back to the raw, unformatted value) rather than erroring, so this needed a
   real generation to catch, not just template inspection.
2. giter8 requires every literal $ in template file content to be escaped as
   \$ - including Scala string interpolation ($id, ${expr}) and Skunk's own
   $-based SQL parameter interpolation ($uuid, $text, $int4). An unescaped $
   that isn't part of a recognized $propname$ reference throws
   "An unexpected error occurred while processing the template. Check that
   all literal '$' are properly escaped with '\$'" and aborts generation
   entirely - caught this via a real generation attempt, not by reasoning
   about giter8's grammar.

Also discovered sbt's own built-in `new` command only resolves a small
hardcoded list of GitHub template shortcuts (scala/scala3.g8 etc.), not
arbitrary file:// URIs, in this sbt version - verification instead uses
giter8's own giter8-launcher library directly (`sbt runMain
giter8.LauncherMain file://<path> --domain_name=... -o <output>`), added as a
project-local (not global) plugin dependency in a throwaway /tmp project, so
nothing about the user's global sbt environment changed.

